# **12. PCA vs t-SNE vs UMAP — When should you use each?**

This is an important practical and interview question.

| Situation                                          | Recommended technique              |
| -------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| Reduce dimensions while preserving linear variance | PCA                                |
| Visualize complex high-dimensional data            | t-SNE                              |
| Visualize large datasets efficiently               | UMAP                               |
| Compress features for a downstream ML model        | PCA or other appropriate reduction |
| Explore clusters in embeddings                     | UMAP / t-SNE                       |
| Preserve interpretable linear combinations         | PCA                                |

### **Important technical distinction**

**PCA is a linear transformation.**

It creates new features using linear combinations of original features.

**t-SNE and UMAP are nonlinear embedding methods.**

They create representations intended to preserve neighborhood relationships.

Don't automatically use t-SNE or UMAP as preprocessing before every ML model. Their embeddings can be sensitive to parameters and may not preserve the information needed for a predictive task.

